<!-- <html>/<body> are ignored - only <body>'s children are copied into the page. -->
<!--
    In-header search box loader for the Oxygen WebHelp Responsive template.

    Loading search-in-header.js moves the stock full-width search band up into
    the header's flex container and stamps `wh_header_search` on <header>, which
    is what resources/search-in-header.css styles.

    Bind this fragment to "webhelp.fragment.after.search.input". Three reasons:

      - it sits INSIDE the search band itself, and the header markup precedes
        the band in every page template, so both elements the script needs are
        already parsed when it runs. Hence no defer/async: the move happens
        before the first paint, with no flash of the tall band.

      - it is included on every page type that HAS a search box - the topic
        page, the tiles landing page and the search-results page. (The
        index-terms page has none, and the script no-ops there anyway.)

      - it is free. Oxygen binds ONE fragment per placeholder, and this
        template has already spent webhelp.fragment.head (dark-mode),
        webhelp.fragment.head.topic.page (GramFrame), webhelp.fragment.
        before.body and .after.body (protection), webhelp.fragment.after.header
        (search flag) and webhelp.fragment.after.body.topic.page (gram-nav).
        Note that webhelp.fragment.header and .footer are NOT free either: they
        are how Oxygen pulls in header.xml and footer.xml.

    The script ships beside this fragment under resources/search-in-header.js;
    Oxygen's custom-resources fileset copies resources/** into the output at
    ${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/, so the src below mirrors
    the path convention the template's other custom scripts already use.

    The <html>/<body> wrapper is not decoration: Oxygen's includeCustomHTMLContent
    copies only <body>'s children when it finds that wrapper, and copies the WHOLE
    document - these comments included - when it does not.
-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <body>
        <script
            src="${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/search-in-header.js?buildId=${oxygen-webhelp-build-number}"></script>
    </body>
</html>
